                                                <h4 class="blog_head exe">1. What is SEO and how a search engine works?</h4>      
                                                <p>Search Engine Optimization (SEO) is the process of increasing the visibility
                                                of your website in the organic search results of search engines. Its goal is to
                                                optimize the website to rank better on the search engine results page and
                                                attract organic traffic.</p>
                                               <p>There are 3 factors you need to remember about how a search engine works</p> 
                                                       <ul class="organic">
                                                          <li> Crawl</li>
                                                           <li> Index</li>
                                                           <li> Rank</li>
                                                       </ul>
                                                       <p style="padding-top: 10px;">A search engine works by crawling hundreds of billions of pages using its
                                                        own web crawlers. These web crawlers are known as search engine bots
                                                        and spiders. The search engine robots will navigate your website and fetch
                                                        web pages to find content. The bot will follow the links that are made
                                                        available on the web pages to find new URLs.</p>
                                                        <p>The search engine bot will store information in the database that it finds by
                                                        crawling web pages and following links. This is called indexing. When
                                                        someone enters a keyword, the search engine will retrieve the most
                                                        relevant results from its stored database.</p>
                                                        <p>The ultimate goal of SEO is to appear on the first page of search engine
                                                        results. The search engine will rank those websites higher because it
                                                        believes they are the most relevant to the search query. It is possible to
                                                        instruct search engine bots to avoid storing or crawling any particular part
                                                        or page of your site for specific reasons. It is up to the bot, however,
                                                        whether or not to cawl.</p>
                                                        <h4 class="blog_head exe">2. SEO basics</h4>
                                                        <p>Understanding the basic fundamentals of SEO is crucial before practising it
                                                        on your website.</p>
                                                        <p>The following are some fundamentals:</p>
                                                        <ul class="organic1">
                                                            <li> Keyword research and targeting</li>
                                                            <li> Relevant content that satisfies the search query</li>
                                                            <li> Crawling your website</li>
                                                            <li> User experience with smooth integration</li>
                                                            <li> Link building</li>
                                                            <li> Schema markup</li>
                                                            <li> Title, URL, and description</li>
                                                        </ul>
                                                        <p>People are likely searching for what you offer in the search engine, and you
                                                        can rank for those keywords. SEO involves three main aspects. That is, on-
                                                        page, off-page, and technical SEO. These three aspects of SEO cover the
                                                        entire field of SEO.</p>
                                                         <h4 class="blog_head exe">3. Keyword Research</h4>
                                                         <p>Now that you understand why it’s important for your website to rank on
                                                            the search engine, let’s look at what keywords you can rank for. A better
                                                            understanding of your target market, what and how many people are
                                                            searching for, and how they are searching for your content, products, or
                                                            services is the foundation of good keyword research.</p>
                                                            <p>Keyword research is the process of brainstorming important search queries
                                                            that your customers might be searching for on search engines like Google,
                                                            Bing, Yahoo, etc. keyword research should be the first step in all SEO
                                                            aspects.</p>
                                                            <p>Analyzing what keywords your competitors are ranking for on the first page
                                                            of Google can give you an advantage. There are various free and paid tools
                                                            available for keyword research, such as Google Keywords Planner, Semrush,
                                                            Ahrefs, Mangools, Ubersuggest, and many more.</p>
                                                            <p>Using these tools will give you an insight into what people are searching for
                                                            in reality, even the keywords that you haven’t thought of, and the volume
                                                            and competition of those keywords.</p>
                                                            <h4 class="blog_head exe"> 4. SEO-friendly Content</h4>
                                                            <p>For your website or page to appear on the top of the Google search engine,
                                                            you need your content to show when a search query is entered on the
                                                            search engine.</p>
                                                            <p>Not all contents will rank. Only content created to show searchers the topic
                                                            they are looking for will be ranked.</p>
                                                            <p>Understanding the search intent is beneficial to deciding whether to go for
                                                            that topic or not.</p>
                                                            <p>It can be anything, post, blog, infographic, product, or landing page. Your
                                                            content should be SEO friendly, meaning it should be optimised in a way
                                                            that satisfies the Google bot and follows the SEO parameters.</p>
                                                             <h4 class="blog_head exe">5. Internal Linking</h4>
                                                             <p>In your content, you should give internal links to another page of the same
                                                                website. Your customers should be taken to another page of the website to
                                                                find relevant content.</p>
                                                                <p>Google will send robots to crawl your website by following links, internal
                                                                links, and external links.</p>
                                                                <p>Internal links are links that connect pages within the same domain.</p>
                                                                <p>A high number of links pointing to a specific page will send a message to the
                                                                search engine bot that the page is relevant. But it should be done in a
                                                                natural way to avoid spamming.</p>
                                                                <h4 class="blog_head exe">6. On-page SEO</h4>
                                                                <p>There is a saying or a joke in the SEO industry that every SEO professional is
                                                                    aware of. That is, “if you want to hide a dead body, hide it on the second
                                                                    page of Google.” Jokes aside, this statement holds true to some extent
                                                                    because your website is as good as dead if it’s not on the first page of
                                                                    Google.</p>
                                                                    <p>Nobody goes past the first page of Google because their query is answered
                                                                    on the first few pages of the rankings. This is where on-page SEO comes
                                                                    into play.</p>
                                                                    <p>On-page SEO is done on the pages of the website. On-page optimization
                                                                    refers to optimising your website’s content. Google will send their bots to
                                                                    search for keywords on your website. Using the same keyword repeatedly
                                                                    will impact the ranking of your website negatively. It is also called “Keyword
                                                                    cannibalization.” Although Google no longer tolerates keyword
                                                                    cannibalization and may penalise your website.</p>
                                                                    <p>Make your URL, title and description attractive to draw more traffic in your
                                                                    website.</p>
                                                                     <h4 class="blog_head exe">7. Link building</h4>
                                                                     <p>You have created high-quality content that satisfies and answers people&#39;s
                                                                        search queries. But quality alone doesn’t mean your page will rank on a
                                                                        search engine. To compete with similar high-quality content, you must
                                                                        obtain links from a reliable source. This will build brand authority and
                                                                        amplify your traffic.</p>
                                                                        <p>To build trust with search engines, you need backlinks from credible and
                                                                        trustworthy sites. Links from popular sites carry more weight and trust.</p>
                                                                        <p>There are two types of links: do-follow and no-follow.</p>
                                                                        <p>Do-follow links are those where search engines are following that link and
                                                                        discovering new pages.</p>
                                                                        <p>No-follow links are those where your links are not followed by the search
                                                                        engine.</p>
                                                                        <p>No-follow links from a popular site can help you gain traffic, but they won’t
                                                                        pass the authority test from search engines.</p>
                                                                        <p>However, the do-follow link is the one where your focus should be. because
                                                                        it passes the authority of the search engine. It simply means you’re telling
                                                                        the search engine to follow the link.</p>
                                                             <h4 class="blog_head exe">8. Technical SEO</h4>
                                                             <p>Technical SEO is a one-time process where you set everything once and
                                                                forget about redoing it again whereas on-page and off-page SEO require
                                                                continuous check-ups and are an ongoing process. Technical SEO in general
                                                                is more difficult than on-page and off-page SEO.</p>
                                                                <p>If you want your site to be ranked in search engine results, your pages need
                                                                to be crawlable and indexable.</p>
                                                                <p>The goal of technical SEO is to optimise your website so that it will satisfy
                                                                the Google bot and index your web pages.</p>
                                                                <p>Technical SEO can be complex and difficult for beginners.</p>
                                                                <p>In technical SEO, you can control or instruct the bot as to which pages of
                                                                the site you want crawled and indexed.</p>
                                                                <p>A robots.txt file is used to instruct the bot which pages of the site you want
                                                                to be crawled and which you don’t want the bot to crawl.</p>
                                                                  <h4 class="blog_head exe">9. How to track and measure SEO results</h4>
                                                                  <p>After implementing SEO for your website, the next step is to track your
                                                                    progress and measure the outcome.</p>
                                                                    <p>Start with a goal for your website.</p>
                                                                    <p>After you’ve identified your primary goal, measure additional metrics that
                                                                    could support your primary goal.</p>
                                                                    <p>Next, evaluate how people are engaging once they have landed on your
                                                                    site. Evaluate their visit based on the following: pages visited, conversion
                                                                    rate, bounce rate, time spent on each page, and scroll depth.</p>
                                                                    <p>Google Analytics and Search Console are free tools by Google. You can track
                                                                    everything from where your customers are viewing your website to their
                                                                    behaviour during interactions with your site.</p>
                                                                    <p>Other SEO metrics that you can track are domain authority and page
                                                                    authority, keyword ranking, number of backlinks, and quality content.</p>
                                                                         
                                                                    <h4 class="blog_head exe">10. Productivity tools for SEO</h4>
                                                                <p>There are many paid as well as free tools on the market for measuring your
                                                                SEO productivity. Some of the most popular AI content generation tools are
                                                                available in both paid and free versions on the market, including keyword
                                                                research, plagiarism checkers, and tracking and analysing customer
                                                                behaviour.</p>
                                                                 <p>Here are the best SEO tools for 2023 SEO productivity for SEO professionals
                                                                and business owners.</p>
                                                                 <p>The best tools for AI content generation are Jarvis (now Jasper), Rytr, and
                                                                Peppertype.</p>
                                                                <p> The best tools for keyword research are SEMrush, Ahrefs, Mangools,
                                                                    Ubersuggest, Moz, Google Keyword Planner, and SimilarWeb.</p>
                                                                     <p>Plagiarism checker tools: Duplichecker, Quetext, Grammarly.</p>
                                                                     <p>Webmaster tool: Google Search Console.</p>
                                                                     <p>Google Analytics for a detailed analysis of your website. Install analysis and
                                                                    register with search engine.</p>
                                                            <h4 style="padding-bottom: 10px;color: #ff6632;font-weight: 600;">What is SEO and how a search engine works?</h4>
                                                            <p>SEO, or Search Engine Optimization, is the practice of improving the quality
                                                            and quantity of website traffic by increasing the visibility of a website or a
                                                            web page in a search engine&#39;s unpaid results. This is done through a variety
                                                            of techniques, such as optimizing the content and structure of a website, as
                                                            well as building backlinks from other websites.</p>
                                                            <p>Search engines like Google, Bing, and Yahoo use complex algorithms to
                                                            determine the relevance and quality of a website&#39;s content, and then use
                                                            that information to rank the website in their search results. These
                                                            algorithms take into account a wide variety of factors, including the
                                                            keywords used on a website, the quality of the content and the number and
                                                            quality of backlinks pointing to a website.</p>
                                                            <p>Search engines work by using special programs called crawlers. These
                                                            crawlers follow links on the web and discover new pages. Once a page is
                                                            found, it gets indexed and added to the search engine&#39;s database.</p>
                                                            <p>So, when a user conducts a search, the search engine uses its algorithms to
                                                            determine which websites in its database are most relevant to the user&#39;s
                                                            query and returns those results. Generally the higher a website is ranked in
                                                            the search results, the more likely it is for users to see and visit it.</p>
                                                            <p>In summary SEO is all about making sure that your website is easily
                                                            discoverable by search engines so that it can be easily found by users
                                                            searching for relevant keywords. Search engines works by crawling,
                                                            indexing and ranking the website based on the relevance of the web page
                                                            to the keywords searched by users.</p>
                                                             <h4 style="padding-bottom: 10px;color: #ff6632;font-weight: 600;">SEO Basics</h4>
                                                             <p>SEO stands for Search Engine Optimization. The goal of SEO is to improve a
                                                            website&#39;s visibility and ranking on search engine results pages (SERPs) like
                                                            Google, Bing, and Yahoo. There are many different strategies that can be
                                                            used to improve SEO, but some of the basics include:</p>
                                                            <h4 style="color: #000066;">Using relevant keywords in website content and meta tags</h4>
                                                            <ul class="organic1">
                                                                <li>Creating high-quality, unique, and informative content</li>
                                                                 <li>Building backlinks from other relevant websites to your website</li>
                                                                 <li>Developing a well-designed and easy to navigate website</li>
                                                                 <li>Optimizing website images and videos</li>
                                                                 <li>Ensuring website speed is fast</li>
                                                                 <li>Making sure the website is mobile-friendly</li>
                                                            </ul>
                                                            <p>Overall, SEO is the practice of making website more appealing to search
                                                            engines, it can help businesses increase traffic from relevant customers.</p>
                                                            <p>SEO stands for &quot;Search Engine Optimization.&quot; It&#39;s the practice of improving
                                                            the quality and quantity of website traffic by increasing the visibility of a
                                                            website or a web page in a search engine&#39;s unpaid results.</p>
                                                            <p>There are many ways to improve your website&#39;s SEO, but mainly it can be
                                                            broken down into two categories: On-page optimization and off-page
                                                            optimization.</p>
                                                            <h4 style="color: #000066;">On-page optimization includes things like:</h4>
                                                            <ul class="organic1">
                                                                <li>Choosing the right keywords</li>
                                                                <li>Creating quality content</li>
                                                                <li>Optimizing images and videos</li>
                                                                <li>Making sure the website is mobile-friendly</li>
                                                            </ul>
                                                             <h4 style="color: #000066;">Off-page optimization includes things like</h4>
                                                             <ul class="organic1">
                                                                 <li>Building backlinks to your website</li>
                                                                <li>Creating social media profiles and promoting your website through social
                                                                media</li>
                                                             </ul>
                                                             <p>Overall, SEO is a long-term strategy that helps your website rank higher in
                                                                search engine results, which in turn can lead to more traffic and potential
                                                                customers.</p>
                                                           <h4 class="blog_head exe">KEYWORD RESEARCH</h4>
                                                           <p>Keyword research is the process of identifying and selecting the words and
                                                            phrases that people use to search for products, services or information on a
                                                            search engine. These words and phrases are called &quot;keywords.&quot;</p>
                                                            <p>The purpose of keyword research is to understand which keywords are
                                                            most important to your business or industry as well as which keywords your
                                                            target audience is searching for. This information can be used to optimize
                                                            your website, content and online advertising campaigns.</p>
                                                            <p>There are a number of tools that can be used for keyword research such as
                                                                Google&#39;s Keyword Planner, SEMrush, Ahrefs, and Moz.</p>
                                                                <p>When conducting keyword research, it is important to find the balance
                                                                between high volume keywords, which are searched frequently and low
                                                                competition keywords which are less searched but less competitive. For
                                                                example, a keyword like &quot;shoes&quot; is a high volume keyword, but it&#39;s also
                                                                highly competitive. On the other hand, a keyword like &quot;handmade leather
                                                                shoes&quot; is lower volume but less competitive.</p>
                                                                <p>Personally, I recommend using a mix of both types of keywords in your SEO
                                                            and content marketing strategy. And also it&#39;s important to keep in mind,
                                                            targeting too many keywords with high volume may not be always realistic
                                                            and targeting low volume keywords may not bring enough traffic.</p>
                                                            <h4 class="blog_head exe">SEO FRIENDLY CONTENT</h4>
                                                            <p>SEO-friendly content refers to the type of content that is optimized to rank
                                                            well in search engine results pages (SERPs). The goal of creating SEO-
                                                            friendly content is to make it easy for search engines to understand what
                                                            the content is about and to ensure that it is relevant to the user&#39;s search
                                                            query.</p>
                                                             <h4 style="color: #ff6632;">Here are a few tips for creating SEO-friendly content</h4>
                                                             <p>Use keywords in the title, headings, and throughout the content but avoid
                                                                keyword stuffing.</p>
                                                                <p>Create high quality, informative and user friendly content that provides
                                                                value to the reader.</p>
                                                                <p>Use alt text for images and optimize the file name with keywords.</p>
                                                                <p>Use internal and external links to help search engines understand the
                                                                context of your content.</p>
                                                                <h4 style="color: #ff6632;">Make sure your website is mobile-friendly and has a fast loading speed.</h4>
                                                                <p>It&#39;s also important to note that, creating SEO friendly content is not only
                                                                    about placing keywords, but it&#39;s about understanding user&#39;s intent, solving
                                                                    user&#39;s problem, providing information and being user friendly. And also
                                                                    avoid creating duplicate content, as it will harm your SEO.</p>
                                                                    
                                                                    <p>Overall, SEO-friendly content is not just about optimizing for search
                                                                    engines, but also about creating content that is valuable to the user, easy to
                                                                    read and understand and that answers their search query.</p>
                                                                    <h4 class="blog_head exe">INTERNAL LINKING</h4>
                                                                    <p>Internal linking is the process of adding links within your website that point
                                                                    to other pages on your website.</p>
                                                                   <h4 style="color: #000066;">Internal linking is important for several reasons:</h4>
                                                                      <p style="color: #ff6632;">1. It helps search engines understand the structure and hierarchy of your
                                                                    website.</p>
                                                                    <p style="color: #ff6632;">2. It distributes link equity (also known as link juice) more evenly across your
                                                                    website.</p>
                                                                     <h4 style="color: #000066;">There are a few best practices when it comes to internal linking:</h4>
                                                                     <p style="color: #ff6632;">1. Use clear and descriptive link text (e.g., &quot;Learn more about our services&quot;
                                                            rather than &quot;Click here&quot;).</p>
                                                           <p style="color: #ff6632;">2. Use anchor text that includes keywords, if relevant.</p>
                                                        <p style="color: #ff6632;">3. Link to deeper pages on your website whenever possible.</p>
                                                        <p style="color: #ff6632;">4. Use a mix of do-follow and no-follow links</p>
                                                        <p>It&#39;s also important to keep in mind, while creating internal links, to not
                                                        overdo it, as it can harm user&#39;s experience. So, use internal linking
                                                        strategically.</p>
                                                       <p>Overall, internal linking is a simple but powerful technique that can help
                                                        you improve the usability, accessibility, and search engine rankings of your
                                                        website.</p>
                                                        <h4 class="blog_head exe">ON PAGE SEO</h4>
                                                        <p>On-page SEO refers to the optimization of individual web pages in order to
                                                        rank better and earn more relevant traffic in search engine results pages
                                                        
                                                        (SERPs). This includes optimizing the content, images, videos and other
                                                        elements of a webpage to help search engines understand what the page is
                                                        about and what keywords it should rank for.</p>
                                                         <p style="color: #ff6632;">Here are some key elements of on-page SEO:</p>
                                                         <p>Title tag and meta description: These are the snippets of text that appear in
                                                        the search results and give users an idea of what the page is about. The title
                                                        tag should include your primary keyword and be less than 60 characters.
                                                        The meta description should be a compelling summary of the page&#39;s
                                                        content and be less than 155 characters.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Headings</b>: Use headings (H1, H2, H3, etc.) to structure your content and
                                                        make it easy to read. Use your primary keyword in the H1 tag.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Content</b>: Create high-quality, informative and user-friendly content that
                                                        provides value to the reader. Use keywords, but avoid keyword stuffing.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Images and Videos</b>: Use alt text to describe the images and videos and optimize the file name with keywords.</p>
                                                        <p><b>URL</b>: Use a short, descriptive URL that includes keywords, if relevant.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Mobile optimization</b>: Make sure your website is mobile-friendly and has a
                                                            fast loading speed.</p>
                                                            <p>It&#39;s important to note that, on-page SEO is not a one-time task, but it&#39;s an
                                                ongoing process. So, make sure to keep an eye on your website&#39;s
                                                performance and make adjustments accordingly.</p>
                                                <p>Overall, on-page SEO is all about making sure search engines understand
                                                what your page is about, and that it&#39;s relevant, useful and user-friendly to
                                                people who find it.</p>
                                                <h4 class="blog_head exe">LINK BUILDING</h4>
                                                <p>Link building is the process of acquiring hyperlinks (also known as &quot;links&quot;)
                                                from other websites to your own website. These links act as &quot;votes&quot; for
                                                
                                                your website and are one of the key factors that search engines use to
                                                determine the relevance and authority of your website.</p>
                                                <p style="color: #ff6632;">There are many ways to acquire links, but some common link building
                                                strategies include:</p>
                                                <p><b>Content creation</b>: Creating high-quality, informative and engaging content that others want to link to.</p>
                                                <p><b>Guest blogging</b>: Writing content for other websites in your industry in
                                                    exchange for a link back to your website.</p>
                                                    <p><b>Broken link building</b>: Finding broken links on other websites and offering to
                                                    replace them with links to your own website.</p>
                                                    <p><b>Directory submission</b>s: Submitting your website to online directories that
                                                        are relevant to your industry.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Social media</b>: Promoting your website and content on social media platforms to attract links.</p>
                                                        <p>It&#39;s important to note that, Search engines like Google, have been putting
                                                            less emphasis on the quantity of links and more on the quality and
                                                            relevance of links. So, acquiring links from high-quality, relevant and
                                                            authoritative websites is important for link building efforts.</p>
                                                            <p>Also, avoid buying links or participating in link schemes, as it will harm your
                                                            website&#39;s ranking.</p>
                                                            <p>Overall, link building is an essential part of SEO, and it can help increase
                                                            your website&#39;s visibility and traffic from search engines. However, it&#39;s
                                                            important to keep in mind that it&#39;s not only about quantity but also the
                                                            quality of links that point to your website.</p>
                                                            <h4 class="blog_head exe">TECHNICAL SEO</h4>
                                                            <p>Technical SEO refers to the optimization of a website&#39;s underlying
                                                        infrastructure, such as its code, hosting, and server environment, to
                                                        improve its ability to be crawled and indexed by search engines.</p>
                                                         <p style="color: #ff6632;">Here are a few important technical SEO considerations:</p>
                                                         <p><b>Crawlability</b>: Ensure that search engine crawlers can easily access and index
                                                        your website by creating a XML sitemap and submitting it to search
                                                        engines.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Mobile optimization:</b> Make sure your website is mobile-friendly and has a
                                                        fast loading speed.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Site Structure</b>: Organize your website&#39;s content in a logical and hierarchical
                                                        manner, using a clear and consistent URL structure.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Canonicals</b>: Use rel=canonical tags to prevent duplicate content issues.</p>
                                                        <p><b>301 redirects</b>: Use 301 redirects to forward old pages to new ones, to avoid
                                                        404s and preserve link equity.</p>
                                                        <p><b>Server response codes</b>: Monitor your website&#39;s server response codes (e.g.
                                                        200, 404, 301) to ensure that pages are properly returning codes and are
                                                        accessible to the search engine spiders.</p>
                                                                                                     <p>Technical SEO can also includes Schema Markup, structured data
                                                        implementation and also website&#39;s security and accessibility</p>  
                                                        <p>It&#39;s also important to keep in mind that Technical SEO is not a one-time
                                                        task, but it&#39;s an ongoing process. Regularly monitoring and auditing your
                                                        website for technical errors and making the necessary fixes can help ensure
                                                        that your website is technically sound and easily crawlable.</p>
                                                        <p>Overall, Technical SEO is a crucial aspect of SEO, as it ensures that search
                                                        engines can easily crawl and index your website, which in turn can help
                                                        improve its visibility and search engine rankings.</p>
